1.79.m:
the very cool flame then becomes tranquil like the rays of the moon;
and a dense flood is formed by the streams of diffused nectar:
one should contemplate the entire assembly of elements as thoroughly flooded by this.

Thus this narrative of Hanumān has been related to you, O Brahmin;
it grants happiness and liberation, and is the essential truth. What else do you wish to hear?

Thus ends the seventy-ninth chapter, entitled “The Deeds of Hanumān”, in the Third Part of the Great Narrative in the First Section of the glorious Bṛhannāradīya Purāṇa.
